{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1368035-what-does-rank-level-6-mean","id":1368035,"title":"What does \"Rank/Level 6\" mean?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-15T07:01:06-08:00","id":1368035,"title":"What does \"Rank/Level 6\" mean?","content":"So we all know it is a legendary level in Werewolf, what does it specifically mean? I can recall rank 6 garou, level 6 gifts, level 6 rites, level 6 fetishes, level 6 caern and so on.<br /> <br /> Rank 6 garou means legendary figures according to W20, and has no specific requirements in Renown. But rank 6 npcs in older books seem too outnumbered and underwhelmed. A comment about them: <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1156649-opinions-on-rank-6</span><br /> <br /> Level 6 Gifts are &quot;blessings of gods&quot; according to W20. But canon ones are totally... passable.<br /> <br /> Level 6 Rites are only several, and all of them are almost... plot device.<br /> <br /> Level 6 fetishes are covered in Hammer &amp; Klaive, they're legend, of course, but also a little passable.<br /> <br /> Level 6 caern... it is almost never mentioned in canon, iirc only an extremely one (the Graveyard of the Lost in Pangaea Realm in Rev. Umbra book , it is level 5 in W20 one). Rites of building caerns in W20 even doesn't have required success for level 5 caern. <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What's your opinion about them? How do you establish them? </span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 02-15-2020, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T10:21:38-08:00","id":1368061,"title":"","content":"Rank 6 for characters actually does have a requirement for Renown, and that's 10 dots in each category, i.e. maxing out Renown. Gifts for this rank are rather wildly inconsistent in effect, much like Gifts in general, but they all have to be learned straight from Incarna-level spirits or higher. One of the more impressive ones even gets learned more easily by one of the Fera - Rokea can learn C'et's Shell one level earlier than Red Talons can get Shield of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Like all things about W:tA, it often seems like something is being held back, either in mention of their capabilities (particularly with Gifts) or in a lot of categories not providing an example (Rank 6 Gifts are not named for each splat axis, just the auspices and a few tribes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T14:28:46-08:00","id":1368133,"title":"","content":"Revised (since it had more room on the topic really) had a decent write-up of the narrative requirements of becoming Rank 6. It's fairly purposefully vague because they don't want it to be something that can be achieved just by having the right mechanics checked off. My two basic criteria are:<br /> <br /> 1) Would it seem strange if a Cliath of your Tribe, or a Fostern of any other Tribe, has never head of you? If yes, you're a Legend. If no, you're still an Elder.<br /> <br /> 2) If you have to seriously ask, &quot;Is my PC a Legend yet?&quot; the answer is probably no.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of what they can do are lackluster, though the point always seemed to be more about powers that are plot devices over being major mechanical boosts. I don't really have a problem with their Gifts being more about what stories their powers drive than strictly being amped up versions of stuff that already exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T23:32:30-08:00","id":1369284,"title":"","content":"So do you have more ideas about other &quot;Level 6&quot; things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T15:08:16-08:00","id":1369454,"title":"","content":"Which other things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avata